<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n12139" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cȳmē</span></b> ,
		ēs, f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Κύμη</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a town of Æolis, near the mod.
			Sanderli</i> or <i>Sandarlio</i>, <i><span class="en">Mel. 1, 18,
				1</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 5, 30, 32, § 121</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Nep.
				Alcib. 7, 1</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Liv. 37, 11, 15</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Vell. 1, 4,
				4</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Tac. A. 2, 47</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cȳmaeus</span></b> , a, um, 
			<i>adj., of Cyme</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Athenagoras,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic. Fl. 7, 17</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fundus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 20, 46</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Antigonus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Varr. R. R. 1, 1, 8</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Col. 1, 1, 9</span></i>.—In
				plur.: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cȳmaei</span></b> , ōrum,
			m., <i>inhabitants of Cyme</i>, <i><span class="en">Liv. 38,
				39, 8</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
